## Problem Context
The `signature` and `signature_contains` rules allow us to filter for functions that match certain parameters and return values, but does not allow us to access or use these parameters. In the `do` section of a rule, we do not currently have a way to update the values of a parameter or change the return value of the matched function.

Orchestrion currently supports `{{ .Function.ArgumentOfType }}`, `{{ .Function.Argument n }}` , and several other template variables as documented [here](https://datadoghq.dev/orchestrion/contributing/aspects/code-templates/#the-function-method). A rule that exists in Orchestrion but cannot be replicated yet in `otelc` is the following in `net/http`:

```
{{- $ctx := .Function.ArgumentOfType "context.Context" -}}
{{- $req := .Function.ArgumentOfType "*net/http.Request" }}
{{- if $ctx -}}
	__ddtrace_client.{{ .AST.Fun.Name }}(
		{{ $ctx }},
		{{ range .AST.Args }}{{ . }},
		{{ end }}
	)
{{- else if $req -}}
	__ddtrace_client.{{ .AST.Fun.Name }}(
		{{ $req }}.Context(),
		{{ range .AST.Args }}{{ . }},
		{{ end }}
	)
{{- else -}}
	{{ . }}
{{- end -}}
```

([full net/http advices here](https://datadoghq.dev/orchestrion/docs/dd-trace-go/v2/contrib-net-http/#getheadpostpostform))

## Request
Similar to the template variable `{{ FuncName }}` already supported by the directive rule, we should have something like `{{ FuncArgument 0 }}` to grab the first (0-indexed) argument of the matched function, `{{ FuncReturn 0 }}` to get the first (0-indexed) return value of the function, etc. 

### Alternatives
We could also consider `{{ Func.ArgumentOfType type }}` and `{{ Func.ReturnOfType type }}` as possible template variables. This could help solve a different variety of problems, but can also be more restrictive if there are multiple parameters/return values of the same type.

**NOTE**
It would also be extremely useful to have access to template variables like `{{ FuncName }}` from all rules, not just `directive`. 

